# BEGIN app-configs syncthing obsidian ignore

# Syncthing ignore rules for Obsidian metadata in any synced folder.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# Obsidian writes per-device UI/runtime state into `.obsidian/` and rewrites it
# constantly and independently on every machine. Syncing those files makes
# Syncthing race against itself and spew conflict files forever. Ignoring every
# `.obsidian/` folder keeps notes syncing while making Obsidian settings local.
#
# HOW SYNCTHING USES THIS FILE
# Syncthing reads `.stignore` from each synced folder root. The FIRST matching
# rule wins, and each child is checked separately. With the leading `(?d)` flag,
# an ignored file may be DELETED by Syncthing when it blocks the removal of a
# directory. `(?d)` is used only for disposable metadata (.obsidian, .DS_Store,
# Thumbs.db). The conflict-file rules have NO `(?d)` and MUST stay above every
# `(?d)` rule, so a conflict file inside `.obsidian/` matches them first: it is
# ignored (not synced) but never deleted by Syncthing, because a conflict file
# can hold the only copy of an edit. Resolve those by hand. Effect: a directory
# deleted on another device stays here while it holds a conflict file, and
# Syncthing reports "contains ignored files". Install this managed block on
# every configured Syncthing folder (see ops/syncthing-obsidian-stignore.sh).
#
# Patterns are relative to the folder root. `**` matches across directories.

# --- Conflict files: not synced, NEVER deleted. Keep ABOVE every (?d) rule ---
**.sync-conflict-*
**sync-conflict-*
**data-sync-conflict.*

# --- Never sync Obsidian metadata folders anywhere in a Syncthing folder ----
(?d).obsidian
(?d).obsidian/**
(?d)**/.obsidian
(?d)**/.obsidian/**

# --- Common cross-tool noise ------------------------------------------------
(?d)**/.DS_Store
(?d)**/Thumbs.db

# END app-configs syncthing obsidian ignore
